WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.436 --> 00:00:04.253
Unit three. Substance Abuse and Addiction Awareness!

2
00:00:05.182 --> 00:00:09.200
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.401
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.451 --> 00:00:17.200
Today we learn about Substance Abuse and Addiction Awareness. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.948 --> 00:00:21.265
Addiction. Say it with me. Addiction!

6
00:00:24.754 --> 00:00:28.404
Dependency. Say it with me. Dependency!

7
00:00:31.915 --> 00:00:35.282
Withdrawal. Say it with me. Withdrawal!

8
00:00:38.776 --> 00:00:42.559
Risk factor. Say it with me. Risk factor!

9
00:00:46.052 --> 00:00:50.002
Prevention program. Say it with me. Prevention program!

10
00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:57.119
Support group. Say it with me. Support group!

11
00:01:00.663 --> 00:01:04.247
Recovery. Say it with me. Recovery!

12
00:01:07.728 --> 00:01:11.612
Healthy coping. Say it with me. Healthy coping!

13
00:01:15.118 --> 00:01:26.960
Addiction can develop into a physical dependency, sometimes causing withdrawal when stopped. Understanding a risk factor helps a prevention program work better. A support group can help someone in recovery build healthy coping skills.

14
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.644
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:31.295 --> 00:01:36.213
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:37.413
Withdrawal!

17
00:01:38.378 --> 00:01:43.341
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:43.391 --> 00:01:44.541
Recovery!

19
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:52.362
Did you know? The brain's reward system, still developing in teenagers, is part of why early substance use carries higher risk.

20
00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.287
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:55.672 --> 00:02:03.913
Think and answer. Why is prevention often easier than recovery from addiction?

22
00:02:03.963 --> 00:02:05.113
Great answer!

23
00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:10.594
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:10.644 --> 00:02:13.096
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

